{"oai_response": {"id": "chatcmpl-a4149adc4ce41500", "created": 1787270864, "model": "nvidia/nemotron-3-ultra-550b-a55b", "object": "chat.completion", "system_fingerprint": "vllm-0.26.0-tp8-6b7faac2", "choices": [{"finish_reason": "stop", "index": 0, "message": {"content": "```python\nimport sys\n\ndef compute_pi(p):\n    m = len(p)\n    pi = [0] * m\n    for i in range(1, m):\n        j = pi[i - 1]\n        while j > 0 and p[i] != p[j]:\n            j = pi[j - 1]\n        if p[i] == p[j]:\n            j += 1\n        pi[i] = j\n    return pi\n\ndef compute_transition(p, pi):\n    m = len(p)\n    trans = [[0] * 2 for _ in range(m + 1)]\n    for state in range(m + 1):\n        for bit in (0, 1):\n            if state == m:\n                trans[state][bit] = m\n            else:\n                c = '0' if bit == 0 else '1'\n                j = state\n                while j > 0 and c != p[j]:\n                    j = pi[j - 1]\n                if c == p[j]:\n                    j += 1\n                trans[state][bit] = j\n    return trans\n\ndef mat_mul(A, B):\n    n = len(A)\n    C = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        Ai = A[i]\n        Ci = C[i]\n        for k in range(n):\n            aik = Ai[k]\n            if aik:\n                Bk = B[k]\n                for j in range(n):\n                    Ci[j] += aik * Bk[j]\n    return C\n\ndef mat_pow(mat, power):\n    n = len(mat)\n    # Initialize result as identity matrix\n    res = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n    for i in range(n):\n        res[i][i] = 1\n    base = mat\n    while power > 0:\n        if power & 1:\n            res = mat_mul(res, base)\n        base = mat_mul(base, base)\n        power >>= 1\n    return res\n\ndef solve():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().strip().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    s = data[1]\n    m = len(s)\n\n    # Build KMP prefix function and transition table\n    pi = compute_pi(s)\n    trans = compute_transition(s, pi)\n\n    # Build transition matrix of size (m+1) x (m+1) for states 0..m, but we will restrict to states 0..m-1\n    # State m is absorbing (accepting). We want strings that NEVER reach state m.\n    # So we build matrix for states 0..m-1.\n    size = m\n    M = [[0] * size for _ in range(size)]\n    for state in range(size):\n        for bit in (0, 1):\n            ns = trans[state][bit]\n            if ns < m:\n                M[state][ns] += 1\n            # if ns == m, we don't add (leads to forbidden state)\n\n    # Compute M^n\n    Mn = mat_pow(M, n)\n\n    # Initial vector: state 0 has count 1\n    # Number of strings of length n that avoid s as substring in linear sense\n    # = sum_{j=0}^{m-1} Mn[0][j]\n    avoid = sum(Mn[0][j] for j in range(size))\n\n    total = 1 << n  # 2^n\n    answer = total - avoid\n    print(answer)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    solve()\n```", "role": "assistant", "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null, "reasoning": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {"stop_reason": null, "token_ids": null, "routed_experts": null}}], "usage": {"completion_tokens": 775, "prompt_tokens": 484, "total_tokens": 1259}}, "source_data": {"prob_desc_input_from": "standard input", "lang": "Python", "src_uid": "0034806908c9794086736a2d07fc654c", "difficulty": 2900, "prob_desc_sample_inputs": "[\"2\\n0\", \"4\\n1010\", \"20\\n10101010101010\"]", "prob_desc_time_limit": "2 seconds", "tags": ["dp", "strings"], "prob_desc_output_spec": "Print the only integer\u00a0\u2014 the number of distinct cyclical binary strings $$$t$$$, which contain $$$s$$$ as a substring.", "prob_desc_input_spec": "The first line contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 40$$$)\u00a0\u2014 the length of the target string $$$t$$$. The next line contains the string $$$s$$$ ($$$1 \\le |s| \\le n$$$)\u00a0\u2014 the string which must be a substring of cyclical string $$$t$$$. String $$$s$$$ contains only characters '0' and '1'.", "lang_cluster": "Python", "source_cod